"""Triton implementation of aten::pinverse (Moore-Penrose pseudoinverse).

Algorithm: one-sided (Hestenes) Jacobi SVD driven by a single Triton kernel with
one program per matrix, followed by the in-kernel assembly
``pinv(W) = V diag(1/sigma^2) B^T`` where ``B = W V`` is the rotated working
matrix.  The working matrix is ``A`` when ``m >= n`` and ``A^T`` otherwise, so
the reduction dimension is always the larger one.

Every per-pair operation is expressed on 1-D vectors with scalar rotation
coefficients (the cyclic round-robin schedule is decoded arithmetically from a
flat pair index), because 2-D gathered loads combined with axis-0 reductions do
not stay numerically correct on this backend beyond k ~ 8.

Reference semantics reproduced (verified against torch.pinverse on this target):
  * sigma_i is kept iff ``sigma_i > rcond * sigma_max``; a zero matrix maps to
    exact zeros;
  * any non-finite input element makes the whole result NaN;
  * empty inputs return an allocated empty result with the swapped trailing
    shape and launch no kernel;
  * rank < 2, unsupported dtype, negative rcond and autograd inputs raise
    NotImplementedError (a subclass of RuntimeError, which is what ATen raises).
"""

